sharpness: odd zero-free map T^k -> R^2 for each k
  k= 1: w_i odd at i=0; odd & zero-free & free: True
  k= 2: w_i odd at i=0; odd & zero-free & free: True
  k= 3: w_i odd at i=2; odd & zero-free & free: True
  k= 5: w_i odd at i=4; odd & zero-free & free: True
  k= 8: w_i odd at i=0; odd & zero-free & free: True
  k=13: w_i odd at i=0; odd & zero-free & free: True
ALL k verified: True

=> ind(T^k) < 2 for every k; with ind >= 1 this gives ind = 1 EXACTLY.
   Contrast ind(S^k) = k: S^k is NOT aspherical for k >= 2, which is the
   entire reason BU works there and collapses on the torus.
